WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.073 --> 00:00:02.334
-Welcome, everyone.
Welcome, welcome, welcome

00:00:02.334 --> 00:00:03.603
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:05.071
You're here.
You're watching at home.

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:07.540
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you for watching.

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:09.141
Let's get to some news.

00:00:09.141 --> 00:00:11.677
Well, guys, yesterday,
the director of the CDC

00:00:11.677 --> 00:00:14.414
appeared on four
Sunday morning talk shows

00:00:14.414 --> 00:00:15.814
to defend the quick reversal

00:00:15.814 --> 00:00:18.884
of mask recommendations
for vaccinated Americans.

00:00:18.884 --> 00:00:20.820
[ Scattered
cheers and applause ]

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:23.289
Yeah. See,
half of the audience is clapping

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:26.059
because I think a lot of people
don't understand the new rules.

00:00:26.059 --> 00:00:27.427
[ Laughter ]

00:00:27.427 --> 00:00:29.962
People -- America
hasn't felt this confused

00:00:29.962 --> 00:00:32.465
since Dunkin' Donuts started
selling avocado toast.

00:00:32.465 --> 00:00:34.934
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:36.669
I don't know what we do.

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:37.703
-Where am I?

00:00:37.703 --> 00:00:38.972
-I get it --
it's a confusing time

00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:41.741
when Best Buy has tougher
health rules than the CDC.

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:43.342
You know?
[ Laughter ]

00:00:43.342 --> 00:00:45.010
That's right --
somehow CDC guidelines

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:46.545
have become more confusing

00:00:46.545 --> 00:00:48.314
than a parking sign
in New York City.

00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:50.283
It's like...
[ Laughter ]

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:51.751
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:51.751 --> 00:00:53.453
"Can I stand here?"

00:00:53.453 --> 00:00:55.321
"No. You can stand here
on Tuesday."

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:56.822
"Oh."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.822 --> 00:00:58.190
That's right --
the director said that,

00:00:58.190 --> 00:00:59.859
for the new guidelines to work,

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:01.561
the CDC is asking Americans

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:04.163
to be honest
about their vaccination status.

00:01:04.163 --> 00:01:07.300
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:09.101
Really?

00:01:09.101 --> 00:01:11.270
People can't even tell the truth
on their Tinder profiles.

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:12.405
You're gonna say -- Really?
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:14.139
Come on.
[ Applause ]

00:01:14.139 --> 00:01:16.575
It was a picture of me.
-Yeah.

00:01:16.575 --> 00:01:18.010
[ Laughs ]

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:19.612
-Meanwhile,
today, even President Biden

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:22.681
tried to add clarity
to the COVID situation.

00:01:22.681 --> 00:01:24.217
I don't think he helped anybody

00:01:24.217 --> 00:01:25.884
dressed as
The Phantom of the Opera.

00:01:25.884 --> 00:01:27.219
I thought that was interesting.
It was like...

00:01:27.219 --> 00:01:28.354
[ Laughter ]
-Wow.

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:29.689
-Now we're doing half-masks.
-Half-masks.

00:01:29.689 --> 00:01:31.924
-We're doing half-masks now.

00:01:31.924 --> 00:01:34.727
♪ Slowly... ♪

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:36.829
-♪ Of the night ♪

00:01:36.829 --> 00:01:38.030
♪♪

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:39.498
-But Biden announced
some good news --

00:01:39.498 --> 00:01:42.035
for the first time
since the pandemic began,

00:01:42.035 --> 00:01:44.437
cases are down in all 50 states.

00:01:44.437 --> 00:01:46.739
So that's...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:48.141
♪♪

00:01:48.141 --> 00:01:49.509
That's great news.

00:01:49.509 --> 00:01:51.811
That's right --
COVID numbers are down

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:54.380
and Instagram posts
of people's brunches are way up.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:56.081
-Aww.
[ Applause ]

00:01:56.081 --> 00:01:58.485
-Look at those eggs. Wow.

00:01:58.485 --> 00:01:59.785
Like!

00:01:59.785 --> 00:02:01.120
Biden also announced plans

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:03.823
to send 20 million
more vaccine doses abroad

00:02:03.823 --> 00:02:05.424
by the end of June.

00:02:05.424 --> 00:02:06.859
You know that -- Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:06.859 --> 00:02:08.194
That's good.

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:10.497
[ Applause ]

00:02:10.497 --> 00:02:12.398
You now that when the vaccines
come back home, they'll be like,

00:02:12.398 --> 00:02:14.434
"It's actually pronounced
'Pfither.'"

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:18.071
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.071 --> 00:02:19.905
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:19.905 --> 00:02:22.007
-I went to "Barth-- Barthel--"
Okay. Alright.

00:02:22.007 --> 00:02:23.476
Alright. Okay. I know.
-How long --

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:24.877
-What's up?
-How long were you there?

00:02:24.877 --> 00:02:25.912
-Two "dayth."

00:02:25.912 --> 00:02:27.680
[ Laughter ]

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:30.049
Two dayth.

00:02:30.049 --> 00:02:31.417
Speaking of Biden, this weekend,

00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:32.785
a "New York Times" report
revealed

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:34.019
what the President is like,

00:02:34.019 --> 00:02:36.489
according to people
who work closely with him.

00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:38.557
They say Biden's obsessed
with details,

00:02:38.557 --> 00:02:42.762
asks many questions,
and displays unexpected warmth.

00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:44.430
It's all part of their plan
to release

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.432
the most boring
tell-all book of all time.

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:48.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:50.370
Oh, wow.
He flosses, too. Oh.

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:51.637
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.637 --> 00:02:53.906
The report also says
that Biden's drink of choice

00:02:53.906 --> 00:02:55.608
is Orange Gatorade.

00:02:55.608 --> 00:02:57.443
-Oh.
-Whoo!

00:02:57.443 --> 00:02:58.511
-Is it?

00:02:58.511 --> 00:03:00.180
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:01.714
Or is it just water
with Metamucil?

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:03.248
[ Laughter ]
Okay, sure, Gatorade.

00:03:03.248 --> 00:03:05.885
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
Gatorade. Yeah.

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:08.954
Apparently, Biden also doesn't
like to be served leafy greens

00:03:08.954 --> 00:03:10.757
'cause he's afraid
of being photographed

00:03:10.757 --> 00:03:12.925
with something in his teeth.

00:03:12.925 --> 00:03:14.227
The White House kitchen
is like,

00:03:14.227 --> 00:03:17.130
"We're now on Year 5
of not serving salad."

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:20.466
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:21.967
Let's change gears here.

00:03:21.967 --> 00:03:23.135
Well, people were
talking about this.

00:03:23.135 --> 00:03:24.737
Last night, "60 Minutes"

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:27.406
had a piece on
the existence of UFOs.

00:03:27.406 --> 00:03:30.476
And this is what a former top
Pentagon official had to say.

00:03:30.476 --> 00:03:37.383
-So what you're telling me
is that UFOs are real?

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:39.084
-Bill, I think
we're beyond that already.

00:03:39.084 --> 00:03:41.186
-It sounds nutty, wacky.

00:03:41.186 --> 00:03:43.622
-I'm not telling you that --
that it doesn't sound wacky.

00:03:43.622 --> 00:03:45.224
What I'm telling you --
it's real.

00:03:45.224 --> 00:03:46.859
The question is, what is it?

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:48.060
What are its intentions?

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:49.796
What are its capabilities?

00:03:49.796 --> 00:03:51.964
-And, of course,
he's talking about his goatee.

00:03:51.964 --> 00:03:54.132
[ Laughter ]

00:03:54.132 --> 00:03:57.070
"What are its intentions?

00:03:57.070 --> 00:03:58.638
Yes, it's wacky.
Yes, it's nutty."

00:03:58.638 --> 00:04:00.073
[ Laughter ]

00:04:00.073 --> 00:04:02.975
"I think it's kind of edgy,
and I'm also in a swing band."

00:04:02.975 --> 00:04:05.645
[ Light laughter ]

00:04:05.645 --> 00:04:08.380
I had no idea
the top Pentagon official

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:10.483
was also in charge of all
the elves in the North Pole.

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:11.550
-Wow.

00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:13.052
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:15.588
-"Hermey doesn't like
to make toys!"

00:04:15.588 --> 00:04:19.792
[ Laughter ]

00:04:19.792 --> 00:04:21.427
All I know is,
if aliens are real,

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:23.529
it means we're a year away
from seeing this.

00:04:23.529 --> 00:04:26.265
-I'm Lesley Stahl.
-I'm Bill Whitaker.

00:04:26.265 --> 00:04:27.399
-I'm Anderson Cooper.

00:04:27.399 --> 00:04:29.768
-And I am Gorgalack 368.

00:04:29.768 --> 00:04:31.370
-Okay. Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:33.839
Guys, today is May 17th,
and you know what that means --

00:04:33.839 --> 00:04:35.241
it is Tax Day.

00:04:35.241 --> 00:04:36.709
[ Audience groans lightly ]
Yeah.

00:04:36.709 --> 00:04:38.211
[ Crowd boos ]

00:04:38.211 --> 00:04:40.212
[ Laughter ]

00:04:40.212 --> 00:04:41.413
-What was that?

00:04:41.413 --> 00:04:43.215
-I don't know.
Yeah, I get it.

00:04:43.215 --> 00:04:45.484
The most popular Google
search today was,

00:04:45.484 --> 00:04:47.953
"Can I write off my home
if it's also my office?"

00:04:47.953 --> 00:04:50.056
and, "Can I write off my bed
if it's also my desk?"

00:04:50.056 --> 00:04:52.391
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.391 --> 00:04:53.759
Since it's Tax Day, can we see

00:04:53.759 --> 00:04:56.628
what the head of the IRS
looks like?

00:04:56.628 --> 00:04:59.365
Yeah, don't worry if you forgot
to file your taxes.

00:04:59.365 --> 00:05:01.000
He looks pretty understanding.

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:03.035
[ Laughter ]

00:05:03.035 --> 00:05:04.804
Can I see him again?
Can we bring it --

00:05:04.804 --> 00:05:06.205
[ Laughter ]

00:05:06.205 --> 00:05:07.473
He looks like his son
just told him,

00:05:07.473 --> 00:05:09.541
"I need 10 grand
for deejay school."

00:05:09.541 --> 00:05:12.811
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:12.811 --> 00:05:14.247
Some business news --

00:05:14.247 --> 00:05:16.949
I saw that Pabst Blue Ribbon
and Entenmann's are teaming up

00:05:16.949 --> 00:05:20.219
to release a new paring
of hard coffee and doughnuts.

00:05:20.219 --> 00:05:21.454
Take a look at this.

00:05:21.454 --> 00:05:22.555
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:22.555 --> 00:05:24.657
[ Laughs ]
-What?

00:05:24.657 --> 00:05:25.858
-What?!

00:05:25.858 --> 00:05:27.559
-And to make it
a truly balanced breakfast,

00:05:27.559 --> 00:05:29.395
just throw in half a pack
of Newport Lights.

00:05:29.395 --> 00:05:31.563
There you go -- that's --
-Wow, nice.

00:05:31.563 --> 00:05:32.765
-Speaking of new products,

00:05:32.765 --> 00:05:34.267
I heard that Mountain Dew
is launching

00:05:34.267 --> 00:05:36.068
a birthday cake-flavored drink
called

00:05:36.068 --> 00:05:38.737
"Mountain Dew Cake Smash."

00:05:38.737 --> 00:05:40.305
Take a look at this thing.

00:05:40.305 --> 00:05:42.474
Yep.
[ Audience ohhs ]

00:05:42.474 --> 00:05:44.910
On the can, the nutrition facts
just say, "Come on."

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:48.247
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:48.247 --> 00:05:49.882
-And finally,
a woman in California says

00:05:49.882 --> 00:05:53.519
she accidentally destroyed
a $26 million lottery ticket

00:05:53.519 --> 00:05:56.054
in the washing machine.
[ Audience groans ]

00:05:56.054 --> 00:05:57.356
When she told lottery officials

00:05:57.356 --> 00:05:59.792
that she lost
a $26 million lottery ticket,

00:05:59.792 --> 00:06:01.260
the guy behind her in line
was like,

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:04.830
"Yes, I also lost
a $26 million lottery ticket."

00:06:04.830 --> 00:06:07.066
Did you guys hear
about Biden's Venmo?

00:06:07.066 --> 00:06:08.433
-Yeah.
-Yes.

00:06:08.433 --> 00:06:10.269
-Did you know that
you can do that?

00:06:10.269 --> 00:06:12.805
You can go on anyone's Venmo --
you see where --

00:06:12.805 --> 00:06:13.939
like, what they spent
their money on.

00:06:13.939 --> 00:06:16.142
-Yeah, it's crazy.
-I didn't know that --

00:06:16.142 --> 00:06:18.077
That seems wrong, doesn't it?
-Yeah.

00:06:18.077 --> 00:06:19.278
[ Laughter ]

00:06:19.278 --> 00:06:20.579
-Well, I guess
"The New York Times" reported

00:06:20.579 --> 00:06:23.116
